Dear Tamara,

I'm not sure why it goes wrong when you use 'i', but S+ must be
looking for an object called 'i' and maybe it finds a wrong one... 

Anyway, the following approach is not relying on finding object 'i' (I
assume you want to do this in a loop):

model.list <- vector("list",0)
for(i in 2:5) 
  model.list[[i]] <- 
    gam(eval(parse(text=paste("y~s(x,", i, ")"))), data=data)

pred.list <- vector("list",0)
for(i in 2:5) pred.list[[i]] <- 
  predict(model.list[[i]], newdata=newdata)

Or you can generate the predictions when you want them:

predict(model.list[[4]], newdata=newdata)

Hope this helps!

Henrik

