On Wed, 2 Feb 2000, Vadim Ogranovich wrote:

[ Do please tell us your S-PLUS version. I am assuming 5.1 here from what
you say. ]

> Dear Community, It seems like any object created and permanently assigned to
> any chapter, but the top in the search list, during a call to For(...) is
> not visible to the calling process until the chapter is explicitly
> synchronized, 
> 
> > For(1, assign("some.weird.name", 1, where=2) )
> > find(some.weird.name)
> Problem: Object "some.weird.name" not found 
> Use traceback() to see the call stack
> > synchronize(2)
> NULL
> > find(some.weird.name)
> [1] "stock3K"
> >
> 
> Is it a bug or a feature? 

A feature. That is what synchronize(n) is for, and For calls
synchronize(1).

> Also is it possible to get the numeric position in
> the search list that corresponds to an object of class "attached" -
> unfortunately synchronize() accepts numeric arguments only?

Yes, of course. match the name slot to the search list. Something like
match(x@name, search()).

