Subject: [S] Hard-copy of on-screen color plot
Message-ID: <Pine.GSO.4.21.0002040914470.4483-100000@newton.gbar.dtu.dk>

Dear S-users,

I think the following trick might be useful to some of you ... or
maybe it's obvious?

When selecting print from the graphics-window started by
trellis.device() under S+5.1 or S+3.4 on UNIX platforms and printing
to a color postscript printer the colors are printed in a mixed-up
gray-scale (at least on HP-UX 10.20).  

If the following commands are put in ~/MySwork/.S.init (S+5.1) the S+
command 'lppsc()' will a color hard-copy. 

assign("lppsc", function()
{
  trellis.color.postscript <- function(...)
    trellis.device(device = postscript, color = T, command = "lp -dpsc2", 
                   horizontal = T, ...)
  invisible(dev.print(trellis.color.postscript))
},
frame=0)

The print command must be set up for your system.

Henrik

