From ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk  Mon Feb  7 12:41:05 2000
From: ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk (Prof Brian Ripley)
Date: Mon, 07 Feb 2000 12:41:05 +0000
Subject: Re: [S] nls question
Message-ID: <200002071241.MAA27364@toucan.stats.ox.ac.uk>

> Date: Mon, 7 Feb 2000 14:16:08 +0200 (WET)
> From: <msvika at mscc.huji.ac.il>
> To: s-news at wubios.wustl.edu
> Subject: [S] nls question
> X-loop: s-news
> 
> 
> Hello, S-plus users!
> I am running nls regression with simulated data (Nsim is for handling the
> number of simulations); sometimes nls algorithm could not estimate
> parametres and it returns me a message
> "the maximum number of iterations exceeded" and stops all future
> simulations.
> I would like to "correct" it: in case that the maximum number of
> iterations exceeded, I would like to receive the last estimator and
> the flag that I have a problem in this simulation and to continue.
> 
> for (isim in 1:Nsim)   
> {
> #data set simulation ...
> param.start _ c(sgsq=sgsq.st, gamma=gamma.st)
> v.hat.fit _ nls( ~ sqrt(wt)*(v.d
> -1/4+(1/(2*pi))*asin(sgsq*gamma^d)),
> start=param.start,trace=i.trace)
> }
> Is it possible?

Use restart: the function try (on 5.x) is a good way to use it.
Something like

for (isim in 1:Nsim)   
{
#data set simulation ...
  param.start <- c(sgsq=sgsq.st, gamma=gamma.st)
  v.hat.fit <- try(nls( ~ sqrt(wt)*(v.d
    -1/4+(1/(2*pi))*asin(sgsq*gamma^d)),
    start=param.start,trace=i.trace))
  if(oldClass(v.hat.fit) != "Error") {
#process results
  } else warning(paste("simulation", i, "failed")
}

