  BR> send e-mail to s-news-request at wubios.wustl.edu with the BODY of the
  BR> message: unsubscribe s-news

I wrote a somewhat more sophisticated version of try() I use in 3.4.  Here's
the help document and the code:

> ?try

Evaluate an expression or return a failure object

DESCRIPTION:
       Returns the value of an expression if it can be evaluated,
       or the fail object if it cannot.

USAGE:
       try(expr, prompt = NULL, fail = NULL, local = T, warn=1)

REQUIRED ARGUMENTS:
expr:     an expression or string to parse  into  an  expression.
       If this argument is not supplied but a prompt is, try will
       prompt for an expression to evaluate.

OPTIONAL ARGUMENTS:
prompt:   prompt string to use if  expr  is  missing.   Prompting
       will not take place if this argument is missing.
fail:     object to return if parsing and/or evaluation  of  expr
       results in an error
local:    the frame  in  which  to  attempt  the  evaluation;  by
       default,  the  frame  of  the  caller of try.  If local is
       FALSE, evaluation is done in the global frame.  Otherwise,
       local can be either a numeric value, interpreted as one of
       the frames of the evaluator, or  it  can  be  an  explicit
       list,  with  the  named  elements of the list defining the
       bindings for the names occurring  in  the  expression.   A
       typical numeric  choice  of  local would be sys.parent(1),
       meaning the routine that called the routine calling try.
warn:     a number used to set the warn option before  attempting
       evaluation.  The  default  value  shows  warnings  as they
       occur.  See the explanation in the help  for  options  for
       details.

VALUE:
       The value of the evaluated expr, or  fail  if  parsing  or
       evaluating expr results in an error.

SIDE EFFECTS:
       The expression given in expr is  evaluated  in  the  frame
       specified by local.  This may have side effects, depending
       on the expression.

SEE ALSO:
       parse, eval, options.

try <- function(expr = "", prompt = NULL, fail = NULL, local = T, warn = 1){
  ## Evaluate expr and return the result.  If the evaluation results in
  ## an execution error, return fail.
  restart(T)

  thisFrame <- sys.nframe()
  if(exists("tryFrame", frame = 0))
        tryFrame <- get("tryFrame", frame = 0)
  else
        tryFrame <- 0

  if(tryFrame == thisFrame){
        if(exists("prevFrame"))
          assign("tryFrame", prevFrame, frame = 0)
        return(fail)
  }
  prevFrame <- tryFrame
  assign("tryFrame", thisFrame, frame = 0)

  old <- options(warn = warn)
  on.exit(options(old))
  if(missing(expr) && !missing(prompt))
        expr <- parse(prompt = prompt)
  if(!is.expression(expr))
        expr <- parse(text = expr)
  if(is.logical(local) && local) 
        local <- sys.parent(1)
  obj <- eval(expr, local = local)

  assign("tryFrame", prevFrame, frame = 0)

  return(obj)
}

