While experimenting with programming with the gui commands, I have written a
small function (see end of message)  which is intended to produce a 3D scatter
plot, with the points coloured according to the level of a factor (which is
not necessarily in the same dara.frame as the x,y,and z variables).

This works up to a point - the problem being that it only permits up to 10
different colours, even though I've requested all 33   which the
documentation says should be available.   If the factor has more than 10
levels, it gives the 11th level the same colour as the 1st.   I'm probably
missing something simple, perhaps in the Options settings,  but, before I go
bananas :-

(i) does anyone know how to persuade   guiCreate("Line3DPlot", . . .     etc
to allow more than 10 colours    ?
      [ I know that with as many as 10 colours to take in, the eye goes a bit
doolally, but on the other hand, if 10 are allowed, why not 11 or 12 ? ]

 (ii) I'd live with the 10 colours, if I could vary the  plotted symbol as
well  -  has anyone done this   ?

but mostly :-
(iii) is there a guide (on the web or elsewhere) to programming with  the  gui
commands   (the Mathsoft documentation on this seems a rather thin )    ?

Any guidance, however peripheral, would be welcome ............

     thanks    Bob Kinley  [ Site Statistician , Eli Lilly & Co , Liverpool ]
................................................................................................................................................................................
The function (so far)

function(X = "S9899", x = "PC1", y = "PC2", z = "PC3", colframe = "T9899", w =
 "Culture")
{
#
# scatter plot of 3 vbles , coloured according to level of a factor (possibly
in a diferent dataframe)#
#
     guiCreate("Line3DPlot", DataSet = X, xColumn = x, yColumn = y, zColumn =
z, LineStyle = "None", ColorExtraColumn = w,
          VarySymbolColorType = "Other Column", ColorExtraDataSet = colframe,
SymbolStyle = "Circle, Solid", NumberOfColors = "33",
          MinSymbolColor = "Black", MaxSymbolColor = "User16")
     guiCreate("MainTitle", Name = "1", Title = paste(X, x, y, z, "  , by",
colframe, w, sep = " "))
     guiCreate("Legend", Name = guiGetGSName())
     invisible()
}

