Subject: [S] Creation of Loop Avoiding Recursive Time Series w/Transformation.
Message-ID: <000701bf74a9$b86cdb20$3a008659@tdowning>

Dear List:

k, a1, a2, and b are scalar parameters.
e is a time series of length n; values of e are known
x is a time series of length n to be recursively created

x[1] == .2
Subsequent values of x are to be calculated by the relation:

     x(t) = k +
            a1*abs(e(t)) / sqrt(exp(x(t-1)))  +
            a1*a2*    e(t)/sqrt(exp(x(t-1)))+ b*x(t-1)

The naive loop would be:

f0 <-
function(e, n = length(e), k = 1e-005, a1 = 0.1, a2 = 0.3, b = 0.5, x1 =
0.2)
{
  x <- matrix(nrow = n)
  x[1] <- x1
  for(t in 2:n) {
     x[t] <- k +
     (a1 * abs(e[t - 1]))/sqrt(exp(x[t - 1])) +
     (a1 * a2 * e[t - 1])/sqrt(exp(x[t - 1])) +
     b * x[t - 1]
  }
  x
}

 I have performed similar tasks using filter
function with method "recursive" before, but I never
done it using lagged transformations e.g exp().  Is there a way
to do this using the filter function and avoid using
a loop?  Thank you very much in advance for any help
with this question!

Thomas J. Downing
Research Assistant
Quantitative Research
Value Line, Inc.

