My question:

> How can I write S-code to calculate the number of observation that fall
> under certain interval of the fitted residual of a linear regression
> regression. For example :
>
> fit.lm<-lm(dep~idp1+idp2,data=A)
>
> if the residual range is between 0.5-2.5, and how can I calculate the
> number of observation (length), mean and standard deviation for every 0.1
> interval of the residual. Any hints? It looked simple but I don't have a
> clue.

=========
by Nick Ellis

Use cut and table or, more generally, tapply
> x<-runif(100)
> xcut <- cut(x,breaks=seq(0,1,by=0.1),include.lowest=T)
> table(xcut)
> tapply(x,xcut,mean)

=============
by Prof. Brian Ripley

cut + table.

=============
by Dr Renaud Lancelot

> mod <- lm(Fuel ~ ., fuel.frame)
> Res <- resid(mod)
> r <- range(Res)
> int <- c(seq(r[1], r[2], 0.1), 1.001 * max(Res))
> attach(fuel.frame)
> for(i in 1:(length(int) - 1)) {
  cond <- Res >= int[i] & Res < int[i + 1]
  temp <- data.frame(n = length(Res[cond]), Resid =
    paste("[", round(int[i], 3), "; ",
      round(int[i + 1], 3), ")", sep = ""),
    Mean = mean(Fuel[cond]), s.dev = sqrt(
      var(Fuel[cond])))
    if(i == 1)
      Result <- temp
    else
      Result <- rbind(Result, temp)
}
> detach("fuel.frame")
> rm(mod, Res, r, int, temp, cond)
> Result
