--------------------CHUCK's answer:-------------------------

Here is a "brute force" solution.  It is not particularly elegant, but
it
works.  If there is a simple solution, I haven't found it.

"matchpairs" <- function(x) 
{
    n <- nrow(x)
    result <- list()
    selected <- logical(n)
    groupNr <- 1
    result[[groupNr]] <- unlist(x[1,])
    selected[1] <- T
    while (any(!selected)) {
      for (i in (1:n)[!selected]) {
            for (j in result[[groupNr]]) {
                thisRow <- unlist(x[i,])
                matchedRow <- match(j, thisRow, nomatch=0) > 0
                if (matchedRow) {
                    result[[groupNr]] <- unique(sort(c(thisRow,
                                           unlist(result[[groupNr]]))))
                    selected[i] <- T
                }
             }
      }
      groupNr <- groupNr + 1
      firstNotSelected <- (1:n)[!selected][1]
      if (!is.na(firstNotSelected)) {
          result[[groupNr]] <- x[firstNotSelected,]
          selected[firstNotSelected] <- T
      }
    }
    result
}

--------------------NICK's answer:--------------------------

not exactly simple, but it works.

