implemented the whole procedure through pasting the different steps
proposed by Chuck in a single function, as below:

> matchpairs2
function(x)
{
        x <- data.matrix(x)
        ux <<- unique(x)
        ix <<- matrix(match(x, ux), nrow(x), ncol(x))
        sets <<- sapply(1:max(ix), function(z)
        ux[find.all.neighbours.of(z)])
        labels <<- sapply(sets, paste, collapse = ".")
        sets[!duplicated(labels)]
