==========================
>>From Andy Liaw <andy_liaw at merck.com

 If I'm not mistaken, the coefficients you get from glm (and lm as well)
for
 a categorical factor does not correspond to the actual levels of that
 factor.  They are the so-called "Helmert contrasts".  I.e., the first
 coefficient corresponds to the difference between the means of year1
and
 year2, the second coefficient corresponds to the difference between
year3
 and the average of year1 and year2, and so on.  For details, see the
Guide
 to Statistics, Vol.1, Ch. 16, page 553.  The discussion is for linear
 models, but I think glm uses the same thing.

 Hope this helps.

 Regards,
 Andy Liaw
 Merck Biometrics Research

